==============================================================================================================
(a) algebra (sympy)
==============================================================================================================
   2 x (dP/dt) x t - eq.9 = 0
   ODE dN/dt = -2 (dP/dt)(N) solved: N_gamma = 6*G**2*N_0**2*omega**3*sigma**2*t/(6*G**2*N_0*omega**3*sigma**2*t + 25*pi);   minus S7 = 0
   eq.9 = 1 photon at t = 25*pi/(6*G**2*N_0**2*omega**3*sigma**2);  minus eq.10 (E_rel = N0 w) = 0   -> tau is the mean time per PHOTON (half a reaction)
   eq.9 = N0 at t = tau_h = 25*pi/(6*G**2*N_0*omega**3*sigma**2);  tau_h/tau = N_0 (= E_rel/w_s, as in SB);  S7 at tau_h: N_gamma/N0 = 1/2
   W = w dN_gamma/dt = 6*G**2*N_0**2*omega**4*sigma**2/(25*pi);  minus eq.11 = 0
   photons expected within T = 1/sig: (1/sig)/tau = 1/(sig tau) -> relative Poisson error sqrt(sig tau)  (B&O: sqrt(sig tau))
   in-out total photons N_gamma,tot = 2 P_tot = 8*G**2*N_0**2*omega**3*sigma/25 = 4*pi/3 /(sig tau)
   fraction of the packet ever converted = N_gamma,tot/N0 = 4*pi/3 /(sig tau_h)
   eq.9 exceeds the in-out total for t > 4*pi/3/sig

